  "title": "A zero-free disk for the minimum cost of a four-edge bipartite matching",
  "batch_label": "primary-20260914",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every pair of integers m,n>=4, assign independent rate-one exponential costs to the edges of K_{m,n}, and let C_{4,m,n} be the minimum total cost of a matching of four edges. Then F_{4,m,n}(t)=E exp(t C_{4,m,n}) is nonzero for every complex t with |t|<mn/4. Moreover, every zero of the reduced numerator of its rational continuation has modulus strictly greater than mn/4. The proof establishes the stronger algebraic statement that the explicit sextic P_{m,n} in evidence/k4-proof.md has no root in |t|<=mn/4 for all real m,n>=4, using F_{4,m,n}=A P_{m,n}/Q for integer parameters. Boundary poles are not claimed to be finite nonzero values. The frozen conjecture for unrestricted k remains unresolved.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
